<div class="text-center py-5">
  <h1 class="display-5 fw-bold"><%= ENV.fetch("APP_NAME", "AdaptableProduct Demo") %></h1>
  <p class="lead text-muted mt-2"><%= ENV.fetch("APP_TAGLINE", "") %></p>
  <p class="text-muted mx-auto mt-3" style="max-width: 600px;">
    Most product strategy collapses because the underlying assumptions were never named,
    let alone tested. Describe your strategy in four fields. The AI surfaces the 8&ndash;12
    most consequential bets embedded in it&mdash;each with a risk rating, a category, and a
    suggested experiment. Re-rate your own confidence on each row. The gap is the data.
  </p>
  <div class="mt-4 d-flex justify-content-center gap-3">
    <% if signed_in? %>
      <%= link_to "Go to my products", strategy_products_path, class: "btn btn-primary btn-lg" %>
    <% else %>
      <%= link_to "Try it free", sign_up_path, class: "btn btn-primary btn-lg" %>
      <%= link_to "Sign in", sign_in_path, class: "btn btn-outline-secondary btn-lg" %>
    <% end %>
  </div>
</div>

<hr class="my-5 opacity-25">

<div class="mx-auto" style="max-width: 900px;">
  <h2 class="h5 text-muted text-center mb-4">Example output &mdash; FieldNote strategy</h2>

  <table class="table table-dark table-hover table-striped align-middle small">
    <thead>
      <tr>
        <th style="width: 32%">Assumption</th>
        <th>AI Confidence</th>
        <th>Risk</th>
        <th>Category</th>
        <th>Experiment</th>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr>
        <td>Solo therapists will pay $39/month without needing a free trial if the weekly view saves them 30+ minutes on claims.</td>
        <td><span class="text-warning">●●●</span><span class="text-secondary">●●</span></td>
        <td><span class="badge bg-danger">high</span></td>
        <td><span class="badge bg-secondary">economics</span></td>
        <td>Offer 10 therapists a direct checkout link before building the full billing flow.</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>Solo therapists are the primary decision-maker and can subscribe without IT or employer approval.</td>
        <td><span class="text-warning">●●●●</span><span class="text-secondary">●</span></td>
        <td><span class="badge bg-success">low</span></td>
        <td><span class="badge bg-secondary">customer</span></td>
        <td>Interview 10 therapists; ask who approved their last software purchase.</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>The weekly review surface is a meaningful differentiator against SimplePractice, not a feature they can copy in a quarter.</td>
        <td><span class="text-warning">●●</span><span class="text-secondary">●●●</span></td>
        <td><span class="badge bg-warning text-dark">medium</span></td>
        <td><span class="badge bg-secondary">competitive</span></td>
        <td>Check SimplePractice's roadmap posts and recent changelog for any mention of session review or weekly summary.</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>Auto-generating a CPT-coded insurance claim from session notes is technically feasible with acceptable accuracy for real billing.</td>
        <td><span class="text-warning">●●</span><span class="text-secondary">●●●</span></td>
        <td><span class="badge bg-danger">high</span></td>
        <td><span class="badge bg-secondary">capability</span></td>
        <td>Build a manual prototype: take 20 real session note samples, generate claims by hand, have a biller review accuracy.</td>
      </tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <p class="text-center text-muted small mt-3">
    AI-generated assumptions are starting hypotheses&mdash;not facts. The point is to disagree with them.
  </p>
</div>

<div class="text-center mt-5 pb-4">
  <% unless signed_in? %>
    <%= link_to "Create your own matrix &rarr;".html_safe, sign_up_path, class: "btn btn-primary" %>
  <% end %>
  <div class="mt-3 text-muted small">
    Open source &middot;
    <a href="https://adaptableproduct.com" class="text-muted">AdaptableProduct</a>
  </div>
</div>
